Package: jmjax
Type: Package
Title: Joint Models for Longitudinal and Survival Data via 'JAX'
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Changbin", "Guo", email = "jmjax.maintainer@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Fits shared-parameter joint models (linear mixed-effects
    longitudinal submodel + relative-risk survival submodel with Weibull or
    spline-approximated baseline hazard) using a 'JAX'/'NumPyro' backend for
    maximum likelihood (adaptive Gauss-Hermite quadrature) and full Bayesian
    (NUTS) estimation. R provides the formula interface, design-matrix
    construction, and summary/reporting; 'Python' (via 'reticulate') provides
    the numerical fitting. Cross-validated against the 'JM' and 'JMbayes2'
    packages; see the package vignettes for methodology and benchmark
    results.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with jax (0.4.30), jaxlib (0.4.30),
    numpyro (0.15.0), numpy (1.26.4) and scipy (1.13.0). Call
    jmjax::jmjax_setup() once to create a dedicated 'r-jmjax' virtualenv
    with these pinned versions, or point reticulate at an existing
    environment that already has them.
Imports:
    reticulate (>= 1.24),
    survival,
    nlme,
    splines,
    stats,
    parallel
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    JM,
    JMbayes2,
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
